// Article 2. Assessments, the late fee, and the lien.
#require "1-association.charter".
Param assessment : Money(USD, 2) = 15000
Param late-fee : Money(USD, 2) = 2500
Fact month Identified by 1..12

Event month-begins Related to month
  Creates assessment-due()
Duty assessment-due Holder owner Claimant association Related to month
  Due within 1
  Terminated by pay-assessment
Fact late Identified by owner * month
  Holds when Held(assessment-due()) For 15
Act pay-assessment Actor owner Recipient association Related to month, usd
  Valid when (usd == assessment && Not(late())) || (usd == assessment + late-fee && late())
Fact lien Identified by owner
  Holds when (Exists month: Held(assessment-due(owner, association, month)) For 30)

Clause 2.1 Approved "34067a7ead6ab7e8f08d8759fd6709c89af2c7e1e8c2f5ae1e239c2919c8925a"
  Norm "Each owner pays the association an assessment of one hundred fifty dollars for each month, due on the first day of that month." => assessment-due, pay-assessment
Clause 2.2 Approved "79779c0171817d29d0617469ffed77acc8eb1c6d0e162eaeaaf1a4f11bf9af76"
  Norm "An assessment not paid within fifteen days after it is due bears a late fee of twenty-five dollars." => pay-assessment
Clause 2.3 Approved "112f0658d0eed6eb7ce5e379d2f2da28e5d99e201b430f0c7a9859b21b9f869f"
  Norm "An assessment still unpaid thirty days after it is due becomes a lien on the owner's house, and the lien remains until the assessment and its late fee are paid." => assessment-due, pay-assessment
.
